- async/generator codegen (legacy BBV; the baseline tier has it)
- remaining unsupported opcodes in legacy BBV: `Eval`, `BigInt`, ES module
  import ops, `using` (the baseline tier compiles all of these)
- module scripts are never compiled by any tier: the shell loads a root
  module through the module loader, which never calls the `scriptCompiled`
  extension hook, so neither the in-process batch nor snapshot
  registration sees module scripts (pre-existing, not new with baseline).
  Register module roots in both flows; needed for full AOT under MIR too.
- move abstract-interpretation transfer func for ops to types analysis
  (currently in emitter for historical reasons)
- use a DSL to write lowering cases and type transfer functions for each op?
  - maybe ISLE?
- `module_is_bigint_free` is weird and we should do better
